{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"**Short answer on the \"expanded\" look: it's accurate, not hallucinated — but your instinct that it doesn't match the native TUI feel is correct, and the mismatch is a deliberate design tradeoff you may want to revisit.**\n\nHere's the chain. `[visible thinking]` is turnbridge's real folding behavior, shipped in the MVP commit two days ago (`49da723`), not something I invented for the smoke test: `src/targets/claude-code.ts:75` folds thinking blocks into a text block prefixed `[visible thinking]`, and `src/targets/codex.ts:51-53` does the same plus `[used tool: …]` for tool calls. What I *did* add yesterday is the smoke seed's thinking turn — I planted one specifically to exercise that fold path (it was item 2 in the checklist), so this synthetic conversation shows the most verbose case on purpose.\n\nWhy it renders \"forcefully expanded\": native TUIs show thinking and tool calls as *typed records* they know how to collapse — greyed-out thinking you toggle open, compact tool widgets. Fabrication can't write those typed records: Claude's native thinking blocks carry cryptographic signatures that can't be forged (the spec marks fabricating them as unsafe), and Codex's reasoning items are encrypted with only plain `message` items verified replay-safe. So turnbridge demotes them to ordinary labeled text — and the TUI renders ordinary text fully expanded, always. That's the \"verbose mode\" feel. It's the product-intent tradeoff: keep the visible record lossless at the cost of native look.\n\nWhat this means in real (non-synthetic) usage, per direction:\n\n- **Codex → Claude** (probably your common case): near-native look. Codex reasoning is encrypted so cledger never captures it — no `[visible thinking]` blocks exist to fold. And the Claude target keeps *structured* `tool_use` blocks, which render as normal collapsed tool widgets. Your Claude screenshot otherwise confirms clean rendering (the literal ``` fence in the grey box is native behavior — Claude always shows user messages raw).\n- **Claude → Codex**: the verbose one. Claude's visible thinking and all its tool calls fold to labeled text, so a tool-heavy Claude session will read as a wall of `[used tool: …]` text in Codex.\n- Same-CLI resumes never fabricate, so never look different.\n\nIf the Claude→Codex verbosity bothers you once you've dogfooded it, the knob to add is a fold-style option (e.g. compress thinking/tool history to one-line summaries, or omit thinking entirely) — but that trades away the lossless-transcript commitment, so I'd wait until real usage tells you it's annoying. Say the word and I'll build it.\n\n**On the model warning:** agreed, and the code already does exactly what you described — it propagates the source's model id verbatim (`actor.id` → the assistant envelope's `model` field), so a user who registered matching external models in Claude Code would get seamless restore with no warning, and everyone else gets one honest notice plus default fallback. I've recorded that as a decided behavior in the design doc's fabrication contract (committed) so nobody \"fixes\" it into substituting a fake recognized id later.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"f68bb92a1a606c5463e35d9f553e5cba8e1f5aeb","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","seq":511},"id":"ev1-349ecc4e6caf60c7708d46730086a53737850158abc0fb1ed7adacfab41d4d47","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-21T23:07:44.482Z","producer":{"session_id":"6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.9.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"**Short answer on the \"ex