{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Done — `--manual` mode is committed, and I left a live fabricated pair ready for you to judge right now. Run these in a normal terminal (not inside a Claude/Codex session, so the TUI gets a clean environment):\n\n```\ncd /private/var/folders/_4/scyv26b567s2jzpwpc6c5zmc0000gn/T/turnbridge-smoke-C8D0Bn && claude --resume 6c97e252-93c0-4ff2-90e8-6bf5a31a72f2\ncd /private/var/folders/_4/scyv26b567s2jzpwpc6c5zmc0000gn/T/turnbridge-smoke-C8D0Bn && codex resume 546c5e01-8168-4be4-820c-f49cb6cf58d5\n```\n\nYou should see four turns in the scrollback: the import notice, the `TB-SMOKE-USER-x4uc9b` / `TB-SMOKE-ASSISTANT-x4uc9b` marker pair, a turn with bullets and a code fence, and an assistant turn with a `[visible thinking]` label and a numbered list. The seed now includes those richer shapes specifically so wrapping/spacing/markdown glitches have something to show up in. Any future run is `npm run smoke:interactive -- all --manual` (or `node scripts/smoke-interactive.mjs --manual`).\n\n**The Claude Code warning, explained:**\n\nWhen turnbridge fabricates a Claude session, each assistant message gets a full envelope including a `model` field, and turnbridge fills it with the model id the *source* CLI recorded for that turn (`src/targets/claude-code.ts:139-141` — it copies `actor.id` from the ledger event). Bridging from Codex, that's something like `gpt-5-codex`; in the smoke harness it's the fake id `smoke-model`.\n\nOn resume, Claude Code restores the session's settings — including which model the session was using — by reading the model id off the last assistant message. If that id isn't a model this build of Claude Code knows, it prints one line:\n\n> Session model smoke-model could not be restored (not a model this version of Claude Code recognizes) — using claude-fable-5 instead\n\nand continues with your default model. That's the whole effect. Nothing is lost or broken — the history renders 